# Startup disk: 1 GiB by default (user-requested floor; FAT16 tops out near
# 2 GiB).  DISK_MB allows a bigger image without editing this recipe -- the
# RimWorld staging script needs ~1.5 GiB because the game is 806 MB of
# apparent size.  mkfs.fat auto-picks the cluster size (32 KiB @ 1 GiB);
# the kernel fat16.c layout math is BPB data-driven
# (bpb_sectors_per_cluster), so no driver change is needed for a larger
# disk.  Stay at or below ~1.5 GiB: past that mkfs.fat has to leave 32 KiB
# clusters to stay inside FAT16's 65524-cluster limit, which the guest's
# FAT driver does not describe.
dd if=/dev/zero of=disk.img bs=1M count=1024
1024+0 records in
1024+0 records out
1073741824 bytes (1.1 GB, 1.0 GiB) copied, 0.350175 s, 3.1 GB/s
mkfs.fat -F 16 disk.img
mkfs.fat 4.2 (2021-01-31)
mmd -i disk.img ::/EFI
mmd -i disk.img ::/EFI/BOOT
mmd -i disk.img ::/boot
mmd -i disk.img ::/home
# CA roots for the browser's TLS stack (libcurl/mbedTLS): the driver pins
# /CERTS/CA.PEM (WebKit/WebProcess/hobbyos/WK5WindowDriver.cpp).  Without
# this every https:// navigation fails at certificate verification and the
# user sees the previous page with no explanation.
mmd -i disk.img ::/CERTS
mcopy -i disk.img certs/cacert.pem ::/CERTS/CA.PEM
mmd -i disk.img ::/nfs
mmd -i disk.img ::/mnt
mmd -i disk.img ::/TESTDIR
mmd -i disk.img ::/tmp
# GB-059: the S2 launcher scans /GAMES for titles (.BIN native ports and
# extension-less/.elf compat ELFs) — games_scan.c / desktop.c:915.  The
# directory must exist on the image or the scan is a documented no-op and
# no compat title can ever be launched by name.  Stage one of each kind
# here so "both a native port and a compat title through the one rig" is
# measurable from a shipped image rather than a hand-staged copy (which
# `make run` would wipe).
mmd -i disk.img ::/GAMES
mcopy -i disk.img obj/intel/xnibbler.bin ::/GAMES/XNIBBLER.BIN
mcopy -i disk.img obj/sdl_test_app_pie ::/GAMES/SDLTEST.ELF
# Selfhost W2 (mtools port): the in-OS acceptance invokes the ported
# build-tools at their frozen /TOOLS/ paths (Makefile.hobbyos sketch).
mmd -i disk.img ::/TOOLS
# L3 (selfhost W-A): VFAT long-name build-payload fixture dirs (mtools-written).
mmd -i disk.img ::/src
mmd -i disk.img ::/src/kernel
mmd -i disk.img ::/src/user_include
